{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d","metadata":{},"source":["> # Topic: 6 Common Beginner OOP Mistakes in Python"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e","metadata":{},"source":["> ### 1) Quick explanation: Common OOP Mistakes\n",">\n","> When starting with OOP in Python, beginners often make the same mistakes.\n",">\n","> **These mistakes include:**\n","> * Using mutable objects (like lists) as default arguments\n","> * Confusing class attributes with instance attributes\n","> * Forgetting `self` in methods\n","> * Using instance methods when they should be class methods\n","> * Not calling `super()` in inheritance\n","> * Putting too much logic inside `__init__`\n",">\n","> *Understanding these mistakes will save you hours of debugging.*"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c3d4e5f6-a7b8-4c9d-0e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f","metadata":{},"source":["> ### 2) Real-world analogy / visual\n","> **Think of these mistakes like common cooking errors:**\n",">\n","> ```text\n","> Mistake 1: Using the same bowl for everyone (mutable defaults)\n","> Mistake 2: Mixing shared ingredients with personal ones\n","> Mistake 3: Forgetting who you're cooking for (self)\n","> Mistake 4: Asking a specific dish about the recipe (method type)\n","> Mistake 5: Ignoring grandma's recipe (super)\n","> Mistake 6: Trying to cook everything at once (heavy __init__)\n","> ```"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d4e5f6a7-b8c9-4d0e-1f2a-3b4c5d6e7f8a","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 1: Using mutable default arguments"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e5f6a7b8-c9d0-4e1f-2a3b-4c5d6e7f8a9b","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> Mutable objects (like lists, dicts) are shared across instances."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"f6a7b8c9-d0e1-4f2a-3b4c-5d6e7f8a9b0c","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class Student:\n","    def __init__(self, name, grades=[]):\n","        self.name = name\n","        self.grades = grades\n","\n","# What goes wrong\n","s1 = Student(\"Ali\")\n","s2 = Student(\"Sara\")\n","\n","s1.grades.append(90)\n","print(s2.grades)  # [90] 😱"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"a7b8c9d0-e1f2-4a3b-4c5d-6e7f8a9b0c1d","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class Student:\n","    def __init__(self, name, grades=None):\n","        self.name = name\n","        self.grades = grades if grades is not None else []\n","\n","s1 = Student(\"Ali\")\n","s2 = Student(\"Sara\")\n","\n","s1.grades.append(90)\n","print(s1.grades)  # [90]\n","print(s2.grades)  # []"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b8c9d0e1-f2a3-4b4c-5d6e-7f8a9b0c1d2e","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:** Never use mutable objects as default values."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c9d0e1f2-a3b4-4c5d-6e7f-8a9b0c1d2e3f","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 2: Confusing class attributes with instance attributes"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d0e1f2a3-b4c5-4d6e-7f8a-9b0c1d2e3f4a","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> Class attributes are shared by all objects."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"e1f2a3b4-c5d6-4e7f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class Counter:\n","    count = 0\n","\n","    def increment(self):\n","        self.count += 1\n","\n","# What goes wrong\n","a = Counter()\n","b = Counter()\n","\n","a.increment()\n","print(b.count)  # 1 (unexpected)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"f2a3b4c5-d6e7-4f8a-9b0c-1d2e3f4a5b6c","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class Counter:\n","    def __init__(self):\n","        self.count = 0\n","\n","    def increment(self):\n","        self.count += 1\n","\n","a = Counter()\n","b = Counter()\n","\n","a.increment()\n","print(a.count)  # 1\n","print(b.count)  # 0"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a3b4c5d6-e7f8-4a9b-0c1d-2e3f4a5b6c7d","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:**\n","> * `Class.attribute` → shared\n","> * `self.attribute` → per object"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b4c5d6e7-f8a9-4b0c-1d2e-3f4a5b6c7d8e","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 3: Forgetting self"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c5d6e7f8-a9b0-4c1d-2e3f-4a5b6c7d8e9f","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> Methods must explicitly receive the object (`self`)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"d6e7f8a9-b0c1-4d2e-3f4a-5b6c7d8e9f0a","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class Dog:\n","    def bark():\n","        print(\"Woof\")\n","\n","# This will cause TypeError\n","# Dog().bark()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"e7f8a9b0-c1d2-4e3f-4a5b-6c7d8e9f0a1b","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class Dog:\n","    def bark(self):\n","        print(\"Woof\")\n","\n","Dog().bark()  # Works!"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f8a9b0c1-d2e3-4f4a-5b6c-7d8e9f0a1b2c","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:**\n","> Every instance method must have `self` as the first parameter."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a9b0c1d2-e3f4-4a5b-6c7d-8e9f0a1b2c3d","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 4: Using instance methods when they should be class methods"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b0c1d2e3-f4a5-4b6c-7d8e-9f0a1b2c3d4e","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> Logic that belongs to the class (not a specific object) is placed in instance methods."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"c1d2e3f4-a5b6-4c7d-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class User:\n","    def is_valid_age(self, age):\n","        return age >= 18\n","\n","# You need to create an object just to check age\n","u = User()\n","print(u.is_valid_age(20))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"d2e3f4a5-b6c7-4d8e-9f0a-1b2c3d4e5f6a","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class User:\n","    @classmethod\n","    def is_valid_age(cls, age):\n","        return age >= 18\n","\n","# No object needed\n","print(User.is_valid_age(20))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e3f4a5b6-c7d8-4e9f-0a1b-2c3d4e5f6a7b","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:**\n","> Use `@classmethod` when logic belongs to the class as a whole."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f4a5b6c7-d8e9-4f0a-1b2c-3d4e5f6a7b8c","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 5: Not calling super() in inheritance"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a5b6c7d8-e9f0-4a1b-2c3d-4e5f6a7b8c9d","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> Parent class initialization is skipped."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"b6c7d8e9-f0a1-4b2c-3d4e-5f6a7b8c9d0e","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class Animal:\n","    def __init__(self, name):\n","        self.name = name\n","\n","class Dog(Animal):\n","    def __init__(self, name, breed):\n","        self.breed = breed\n","\n","# name is not set\n","# dog = Dog(\"Buddy\", \"Labrador\")\n","# print(dog.name)  # AttributeError"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"c7d8e9f0-a1b2-4c3d-4e5f-6a7b8c9d0e1f","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class Animal:\n","    def __init__(self, name):\n","        self.name = name\n","\n","class Dog(Animal):\n","    def __init__(self, name, breed):\n","        super().__init__(name)\n","        self.breed = breed\n","\n","dog = Dog(\"Buddy\", \"Labrador\")\n","print(dog.name)   # Buddy\n","print(dog.breed)  # Labrador"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d8e9f0a1-b2c3-4d4e-5f6a-7b8c9d0e1f2a","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:**\n","> Always call `super().__init__()` when extending a parent class."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e9f0a1b2-c3d4-4e5f-6a7b-8c9d0e1f2a3b","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Mistake 6: Putting too much logic inside __init__"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f0a1b2c3-d4e5-4f6a-7b8c-9d0e1f2a3b4c","metadata":{},"source":["> **Problem:**\n","> `__init__` becomes messy and hard to test."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ❌ Wrong\n","class Order:\n","    def __init__(self, price):\n","        self.price = price\n","        self.tax = price * 0.15\n","        self.total = price + self.tax\n","        print(\"Order created\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# ✅ Fix\n","class Order:\n","    def __init__(self, price):\n","        self.price = price\n","\n","    def calculate_total(self):\n","        tax = self.price * 0.15\n","        return self.price + tax\n","\n","order = Order(100)\n","print(order.calculate_total())  # 115.0"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c3d4e5f6-a7b8-4c9d-0e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f","metadata":{},"source":["> **Rule:**\n","> `__init__` should **only set data**, not do heavy work."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d4e5f6a7-b8c9-4d0e-1f2a-3b4c5d6e7f8a","metadata":{},"source":["> ## Quick mental checklist (remember this 🔒)\n",">\n","> * ❌ Mutable defaults → use `None`\n","> * ❌ Class attributes for per-object data\n","> * ❌ Missing `self`\n","> * ❌ Wrong method type (instance vs class)\n","> * ❌ Forgetting `super()`\n","> * ❌ Heavy logic in `__init__`"]}]}